From: Jiajia Zhang <isaaronzhang@icloud.com>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 03:16:59 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Offer a minimized window whose subrole reads AXDialog (#1670)

* Offer a minimized window whose subrole reads AXDialog

Finder and Transmission report a minimized window as AXDialog instead of
AXStandardWindow, and back to standard once restored, so a standard-subrole
test dropped exactly the rows a switcher exists for.

WindowSwitchPolicy now takes a standard window, or a minimized one that still
reports a minimize button. A sheet cannot minimize, so the button keeps real
dialogs out, and the autoclosure skips the read for a standard window.

* Keep the switch policy comment under the 100-column cap

---------

Co-authored-by: abue-ammar <iabueammar@gmail.com>
